# =============================================================================
# Clarity desktop (Tauri + Vite) — environment template
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env.local` in THIS folder (same directory as this file):
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Then replace the placeholder values with your Supabase project credentials.
# Vite loads ONLY `apps/desktop/.env.local` — there is no `.env` at the repo root.
#
# Where to find values:
#   Supabase Dashboard → your project → Project Settings → API
#   - Project URL     → VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#   - anon public key → VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY  (or "publishable" key in newer UI)
#
# After editing, restart `pnpm dev` / `npm run dev` so Vite picks up changes.
# =============================================================================

# --- Required for auth, Boundaries, goals, custom blocking rules, etc. ---

# Example shape: https://xxxxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co

# Long JWT-like string starting with eyJ... OR sb_publishable_... (Supabase API keys page)
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_anon_or_publishable_key_here

# =============================================================================
# Optional (dev / Tauri)
# =============================================================================
# TAURI_DEV_HOST= — only if you customize Vite dev server host (see vite.config.ts)
